Z||000000||olliver||04-02-2001||11:40 PM||||I am just about to under go a HUGE engine rebuild (2.8L).  The guy who's doing it wants to know what the max h.p. that the computer can handle?...will it go into shut down?...<BR>If anyone has ANY info this would be great.<P>I was guaranteed 220 h.p. but i don't want the computer to crash.<P>Thanx <BR>Olliver||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||04-03-2001||12:12 AM||||First welcome to the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by olliver:<BR><B><BR>I was guaranteed 220 h.p. but i don't want the computer to crash.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>220HP out of a 2.8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Wow if you can get that I would be amazed.  The 2.8 is only a 140HP in stock form so your rebuild will gain you 80 HP that is over a 50% gain.  Get that guarantee in writing!!!!!!!!!  I am not an expert on the subject but a stock computer will handle that. Often 3.4L out of a Camaro are dropped in without problem, these even aren't 220HP.  All I know of in the computer is a rev limiter, nothing exactly about HP.  ||||reg||1
