Z||000009||terryk||04-03-2001||02:38 AM||||The stock ECM will likely run out of range in the 250 HP range. The stock calibrations will run out far below that, around 180-200 or so. Beyond that, the AFR will be so lean that melted parts are in sight. <P>Figure that the stock cals are 12:1 AFR for 2.8L at 5500 RPM. Increase the air ingested and the AFR must go up accordingly. The ECM don't know the air increased, it's assuming you are sucking in 2.8L of air (390 CFM?). But your's sucking in more, so there is less fuel per air sucked in. Leaner. Hotter. Melting.....<P>You won't be running a 200HP engine on the stock calibrations and have it run right. Closed loop BLM will be against the ceiling and WOT will be too lean.<P>According to GM, 300HP is the limit with 12.5:1 compression and race gas with no regard for driveability. I consider over 200 HP without blowing on it, with street gas, to be the same as alien abduction in odds of being true. A 3.4L OHV at it's extreme might hit 210 HP without SERIOUS work.<P>Oh, your last question. The ECM won't crash, the engine will burn up or run crappy. You'll know when both happen.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||07:59 AM||||you'll be fine.. ditch the stock injectors of course, the throttle body and get the Chris West long tube headers. if your gunna be pushing losts of air you'll need to get it out quick. I've got shaved heads, new injectors, an MSD 6A - coil, and a few other thing i'm pushing 154 at the wheels. through an atuomatic. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstdyno_manymods.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstdyno_manymods.jpg</A> <P>i'm sure cleaning up the heads would help a bit but like somone else dsaid get that 220hp in writing. once you do get the car to gether be sure you go to <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>  and find a dyno center near you... I'll see if i can't pull some strings and get you a deal on the runs. just so you can see how much HP you REALLY have. <P>Your computer will be fine.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
